<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "report.conforms-driven CLI exit code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The CLI's quiet-mode output and process exit code are now derived directly from the validation report's own `conforms` boolean, not from a CLI-local violation count. Before: quiet mode printed \"conforms\" / \"<violation-count> violation(s)\" based on `(> violation-count 0)`, and the exit code was `(if (> violation-count 0) 1 0)`. After (commit b14fe6b, \"2 left\"): quiet mode prints \"conforms\" / \"<total-count> result(s)\" based on `(. report conforms)`, and the exit code is `(if (. report conforms) 0 1)` with the explicit comment \"Exit code: conforms=0, not-conforms=1\". This removes a second, CLI-side notion of conformance that could drift from the engine's authoritative determination. Evidence: cli/main.slop diff in commit b14fe6bfca792ae4b9799d14af7cb5235e4893b8." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T01:40:39Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "report.conforms-driven CLI exit code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/23e113e6-02a7-49a8-ade9-2032cf006e02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/a7290189-c9f3-42c3-815b-916d4cf8f323> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF 1.2 triple term support in Rust FFI bindings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Rust crate's FFI layer now exhaustively supports RDF 1.2 / RDF-star quoted-triple terms, closing a gap where the safe Rust API could not represent a `term-triple` value even though slop-rdf's C-side `Term` sum type and Snarl's own SLOP source already handled it (per the earlier \"RDF 1.2 quoted-triple Term support\" decision, which updated only src/constraints/string.slop and src/report.slop). Before this commit, rust/src/ffi.rs's `RdfTermTag` enum had only Iri/Blank/Literal (no Triple tag) and `RdfTermData` had no `term_triple` union arm, so a triple term crossing the FFI boundary had no representation on the Rust side.\n\nThis commit adds: `RdfTermTag::Triple = 3` and `RdfTermData::term_triple: *mut RdfTriple` (rust/src/ffi.rs); an extern binding `rdf_make_triple_term(arena, RdfTriple) -> RdfTerm` plus a safe wrapper `Arena::make_triple_term` (rust/src/lib.rs:213); a new `Term::Triple(Box<Triple<'a>>)` variant (rust/src/lib.rs:242) handled in `Term::from_ffi` (asserts the union payload pointer is non-null before dereferencing), `term_to_ffi` (recursively converts subject/predicate/object and calls `make_triple_term`), and `Display`; and a matching `OwnedTerm::Triple(Box<OwnedTriple>)` variant with its own `From<Term>` and `Display` impls. A new integration test, `rdf12_triple_term_round_trip` (rust/tests/integration.rs), builds a triple term via the arena and asserts it round-trips through `Term::from_ffi` correctly.\n\nThe Makefile/Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock/slop.toml version bump 0.4.0 -> 0.4.1 in the same commit marks this as a patch-level bug fix release, consistent with the commit message \"minor fix for rust ffi\" describing a gap-closing fix rather than new functionality." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T22:57:36Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2b28647f-be58-4f23-9d67-05bb5a944e80> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF 1.2 triple term support in Rust FFI bindings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sh:closed scoped to own property shapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "sh:closed's allowed-paths set is computed, per node shape, as the union of that node shape's own directly-declared property-shape paths plus any sh:ignoredProperties paths — not paths inherited transitively through sh:node/sh:and/other shape references. Implemented in evaluate-node-shape-cached (src/engine.slop): for each `con-closed true ignored-paths` constraint, allowed-paths is built by pushing `(. ps path)` for every property shape on `shape`, then appending each ignored path, before calling `check-closed`. This is the wiring of the previously-unwired sh:closed/sh:ignoredProperties constraints (the \"other\" module) into the node-shape evaluation loop. Evidence: src/engine.slop / csrc/src/slop_engine.c diff in commit b14fe6bfca792ae4b9799d14af7cb5235e4893b8." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T01:40:39Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "sh:closed scoped to own property shapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30bece90-e379-4676-a5bf-260e122a591e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/fe61d83c-d866-4161-8524-f494504f1b8b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Streaming Turtle-to-SnarlDataGraph CLI loading for the data file" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The CLI (cli/main.slop) now loads the data-graph file through a new `load-data-graph` function that streams triples directly into a `SnarlDataGraph` via a new callback-based parser entry point, `parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple` (imported from the `ttl` module), instead of first parsing into a general `Graph` (via the existing `parse-ttl-file`) and then converting that into an `IndexedGraph` the way `load-graph` still does. load-data-graph's callback is `(fn ((t Triple)) (set! dg (snarl-data-graph-add arena dg t)))`, so triples are indexed into SnarlDataGraph's sp/po/p-subjects/p-objects sets as they stream out of the parser, with no intermediate general-graph allocation for the (often much larger) data file.\n\nThis streaming path is applied ONLY to the data-graph file. The shapes-graph file still goes through the original `load-graph` (parse-ttl-file -> Graph -> IndexedGraph) path, because `parse-shapes-graph` (src/parse.slop) still consumes IndexedGraph. main's validate call site was updated from `(match (load-graph arena data-path quiet) ...)` to `(match (load-data-graph arena data-path quiet) ...)`, while the shapes-file load call site is unchanged (`load-graph`).\n\nWhy: this is PR #4 \"fast-parser\", commit 663cff306a0cfd6876d5415b280473abefa4fead — the CLI is the primary place large data graphs enter Snarl, so avoiding the general-Graph intermediate and its IndexedGraph conversion for the data file is where the \"fast parser\" name's benefit is realized end-to-end. Evidence: cli/main.slop diff — new `load-data-graph` function, `(import data-graph (SnarlDataGraph snarl-data-graph-create snarl-data-graph-add snarl-data-graph-size))`, `(import ttl (parse-ttl-file parse-ttl-file-for-each-triple TtlFileError))`, and the `load-graph`/`load-data-graph` call-site split." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T19:18:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Streaming Turtle-to-SnarlDataGraph CLI loading for the data file" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5aab210d-21d1-4c74-a8f0-093a3c72d4aa> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/3d703aaf-ea60-489d-8c12-a498713b8fd2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cached class-membership index for sh:class evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The validation engine now builds a single `target_ClassIndex` (via `target_build_class_index(arena, data_graph, shapes_graph)`) once per top-level `validate()` call and threads it down through the whole shape-evaluation call graph, instead of leaving each sh:class-related check to recompute class-membership/subclass reasoning independently.\n\ncsrc/src/slop_engine.c (transpiled from src/engine.slop) adds `_cached` variants of every function in the recursive evaluation chain — `snarl_evaluate_shape_against_node_cached`, `snarl_property_shape_conforms_cached`, `snarl_evaluate_node_shape_cached`, `snarl_evaluate_property_shape_cached`, `snarl_evaluate_constraint_cached`, `snarl_evaluate_constraint_for_property_cached` — each taking a `target_ClassIndex class_index` parameter that is threaded straight through instead of being rebuilt at each level. `snarl_engine_validate` (the entry point behind `validate`/`validate-with-config`, which iterates every focus node and shape in one pass) builds `class_index` exactly once at the top and passes it into `snarl_evaluate_node_shape_cached` for every focus node, so the whole run shares one index. The original public entry points (`snarl_evaluate_shape_against_node`, `snarl_property_shape_conforms`, `snarl_evaluate_node_shape`) are preserved as thin wrappers that build a fresh `class_index` and delegate to the `_cached` variant, keeping the existing single-shape-eval C API signatures unchanged.\n\nWhy: this is PR #3 \"performance\", commit body \"Optimize sh:class validation with cached class membership index\" — the explicit, stated goal is avoiding repeated class-membership computation across sh:class checks during a validation run. The same commit updates the README benchmark table (cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py results), consistent with a re-measured performance pass, though the fixture set and sizes also changed in this commit so a precise before/after delta isn't directly attributable to this change alone from the diff.\n\nEvidence: csrc/src/slop_engine.c diff — new `target_ClassIndex` forward declarations, the six `_cached` function signatures, and `target_build_class_index` call sites added in `snarl_evaluate_shape_against_node`, `snarl_property_shape_conforms`, and `snarl_engine_validate`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-28T22:30:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Cached class-membership index for sh:class evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Direct term-set fast path for simple-predicate property shapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "src/engine.slop's evaluate-property-shape-cached now branches on the property shape's path shape before evaluating: when the path is a bare `path-predicate`, it calls a new `evaluate-simple-predicate-property-shape-cached`, which looks up the value set directly via `snarl-data-graph-object-set data-graph focus-node pred` (a Set[Term] from the SnarlDataGraph sp index) instead of calling the general `resolve-path`. It only materializes that set into a `List Term` (via the new `optional-term-set-to-list` helper) for the specific constraint implementations that require list semantics; a new `optional-term-set-size` helper gets the value count without materializing anything. Any other path shape (sequence, inverse, alternative, zeroOrMore, etc.) still falls through to the original resolve-path-based branch inside evaluate-property-shape-cached.\n\nWhy: the code comment on evaluate-simple-predicate-property-shape-cached states the rationale directly: \"Simple predicate paths dominate the benchmark fixtures. They can evaluate directly against the object set and only allocate a value list for constraints whose existing implementation requires list semantics.\" This is PR #4 \"fast-parser\", commit 663cff306a0cfd6876d5415b280473abefa4fead. Evidence: src/engine.slop diff adding optional-term-set-size, optional-term-set-to-list, evaluate-simple-predicate-property-shape-cached, and the `(match path ((path-predicate pred) (evaluate-simple-predicate-property-shape-cached ...)) (_ ...))` dispatch at the top of evaluate-property-shape-cached." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T19:18:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Direct term-set fast path for simple-predicate property shapes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/5d691b46-2a0c-4395-a10c-8eec7fc334b4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/704a1d64-5a43-4502-b5cc-71124bc37be4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/2d7239ea-1381-4f11-b577-d247b3803ce0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7cbce4e9-e0e9-4c6c-885f-e5906919dea3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7cbce4e9-e0e9-4c6c-885f-e5906919dea3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SnarlDataGraph as the validation engine's data representation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7cbce4e9-e0e9-4c6c-885f-e5906919dea3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7cbce4e9-e0e9-4c6c-885f-e5906919dea3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Snarl's validation engine (src/engine.slop, src/target.slop) now operates on a new purpose-built `SnarlDataGraph` type (src/data-graph.slop) instead of the general-purpose `IndexedGraph` from slop-rdf. SnarlDataGraph carries four term-set indexes built during triple insertion — sp (subject->predicate->Set[object]), po (predicate->object->Set[subject]), p-subjects (predicate->Set[subject]), p-objects (predicate->Set[object]) — using Set rather than List so membership/dedup during insertion and lookup is O(1)-ish instead of O(n) list scans.\n\nEvery function in the recursive shape-evaluation call graph was migrated from an `IndexedGraph` parameter to `SnarlDataGraph`: evaluate-shape-against-node(-cached), property-shape-conforms(-cached), engine-validate, evaluate-node-shape(-cached), evaluate-property-shape(-cached), evaluate-constraint(-cached), and their C counterparts in csrc/src/slop_engine.c. src/target.slop's build-class-index, resolve-targets, and the ClassIndex type itself were migrated the same way, and ClassIndex gained a new `entry-map (Map Term TermSet)` field alongside its historical `entries (List ClassInstances)` field for O(1) class-membership lookup.\n\nThe original public API is preserved rather than broken: `validate`/`validate-with-config` (C names snarl_validate / snarl_validate_with_config, taking IndexedGraph) now convert internally via a new `snarl-data-graph-from-indexed` and delegate to new `validate-data-graph`/`validate-data-graph-with-config` (C names snarl_validate_data_graph / snarl_validate_data_graph_with_config), which take SnarlDataGraph directly. A new `conforms-data-graph` (snarl_conforms_data_graph) mirrors `conforms`. Callers who can build a SnarlDataGraph directly (e.g. via the CLI's streaming Turtle loader) skip the IndexedGraph round-trip entirely.\n\nengine-validate also gains a per-validation-run `TargetCache` (target-cache-create / resolve-targets-cached in src/target.slop), memoizing sh:targetClass and implicit-class target expansion in a `Map Term TermList`, mirroring the existing per-run ClassIndex caching pattern from the prior \"Cached class-membership index for sh:class evaluation\" decision but applied to target resolution instead of sh:class checking.\n\nWhy: this is PR #4 \"fast-parser\" / \"Fast parser\", commit 663cff306a0cfd6876d5415b280473abefa4fead, merging branch Trivyn/fast-parser. The Makefile SNARL_VERSION bump 0.3.1->0.4.0 and the refreshed README benchmark table in the same commit are consistent with a deliberate, measured performance release built around this new data structure.\n\nEvidence: src/data-graph.slop (new file, SnarlDataIndex/SnarlDataGraph types and snarl-data-graph-* functions); src/engine.slop and src/target.slop diffs (IndexedGraph -> SnarlDataGraph across the whole eval chain, new TargetCache); src/snarl.slop diff (validate-with-config now does `(let ((fast-data (snarl-data-graph-from-indexed arena data-graph))) (validate-data-graph-with-config arena fast-data shapes-graph config))`, new validate-data-graph/validate-data-graph-with-config/conforms-data-graph exports); include/snarl.h and rust/src/lib.rs,ffi.rs diffs (new SnarlDataGraph FFI surface)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
