<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sh:resultMessage serialized in report-to-graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "report-to-graph (src/report.slop) now emits an sh:resultMessage triple for each ValidationResult whose optional `message` field is present. A new `(match (. r message) ((some msg) (let ((msg-pred (make-iri arena \"http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#resultMessage\"))) (set! g (indexed-graph-add arena g (make-triple arena result-node msg-pred (make-literal arena msg (none) (none))))))) ((none) (do)))` block was added right after the existing result-path match block. Before this commit, the RDF-graph serialization silently dropped the message field entirely, even though the sibling human-readable serializers (report-to-string, print-report) already printed \"  Message: {msg}\" when present — so machine consumers of the graph-shaped report (report-to-graph / snarl_report_to_graph) were missing information that text consumers already had. Evidence: src/report.slop diff in commit eae071451c290d38f9aae46264fbb281a11eacf6." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T06:53:07Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9676ef5e-9b5b-4079-b70b-7470fa5e5f8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "sh:resultMessage serialized in report-to-graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SLOP-authored, pre-transpiled C distribution" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Snarl's source is authored in SLOP (src/, cli/) but the repository ships pre-transpiled C sources (csrc/src/, csrc/runtime/) as the primary build path — `make` builds directly from csrc/ with only a C compiler, no SLOP toolchain required. The SLOP toolchain is only needed to regenerate csrc/ from the .slop sources (`make slop-build` invokes `slop build`; `make csrc` runs csrc/update_bootstrap.sh). Evidence: Makefile header comment \"Build from transpiled C sources — no SLOP toolchain required\"; README.md Quick Start \"Build from pre-transpiled C (no SLOP toolchain needed)\"; csrc/generate_c.py and csrc/update_bootstrap.sh introduced in this commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SLOP-authored, pre-transpiled C distribution" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2d0c8898-a534-4606-b0d3-980c57f81eb2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bff330ee-8734-4664-896d-0dbb758002e5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/849132c8-d4d1-45d4-ac28-70f7e47e2fac> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inline property-shape members in logical/sh:node constraints" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "sh:not/sh:and/sh:or/sh:xone/sh:node constraints now correctly evaluate a shape-ref that resolves to an inline PropertyShape (e.g. a blank-node branch like `[ sh:path ex:a ; sh:class ex:A ]`), instead of silently mis-evaluating it. The fix spans two files that had to change together:\n\n1. src/parse.slop: `register-inline-shapes` gains a new `shape-has-path` helper (true iff the referenced blank node declares sh:path). When processing a ref queued from con-not/con-and/con-or/con-xone/con-node, it now branches on `shape-has-path` — if true, the ref is routed to the property-shape queue/map (parsed via parse-property-shape) instead of being parsed via parse-node-shape. Before this commit, EVERY such ref was parsed via parse-node-shape regardless of whether it was actually a property shape; parse-node-shape ignores sh:path/sh:class and finds none of the predicates it looks for (sh:targetClass, sh:property, etc.), so an inline property-shape branch was silently registered as an empty, constraint-free NodeShape.\n\n2. src/engine.slop: a new `property-shape-conforms` function (:c-name snarl_property_shape_conforms) evaluates a node against a PropertyShape by calling evaluate-property-shape with a fresh visited set, returning true iff there are zero results — vacuously true when the shape's path yields no value nodes, per SHACL semantics that a shape producing no violations conforms. evaluate-constraint's con-not/con-and/con-or/con-xone/con-node arms now check `shapes-graph property-shape-map` FIRST and call property-shape-conforms; only when the ref is absent from property-shape-map do they fall back to the old shape-map/evaluate-shape-against-node path.\n\nTogether these fix a real correctness bug: because (1) meant an inline property-shape branch was always registered as an empty NodeShape, and the OLD engine.slop only ever consulted shape-map (found the empty NodeShape as `(some ref-shape)`), evaluate-shape-against-node on that empty shape always returned zero violations — so any sh:or/sh:and/sh:not/sh:xone/sh:node branch written as an inline property shape ALWAYS silently conformed, regardless of the actual data, masking genuine violations. Evidence: src/parse.slop diff (new shape-has-path, restructured register-inline-shapes routing); src/engine.slop diff (new property-shape-conforms, and the `(match (map-get (. shapes-graph property-shape-map) ref) ((some ref-ps) (property-shape-conforms ...)) ((none) <old shape-map lookup>))` restructuring across all five constraint arms). New regression fixtures cli/tests/fixtures/vacuous-or-{data,shapes}.ttl, exercised by cli/tests/test-cli.slop's test-vacuous-or: 3 of 4 focus nodes conform (one vacuously, two via one branch each) and exactly 1 (the node with wrong values on both branches) violates — this would previously have been 0 violations under the old always-conforms bug." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:07:26Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Inline property-shape members in logical/sh:node constraints" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c5a38b0c-b8dd-4141-9d6c-1fa48289a94a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/be181a8d-0d96-4c21-95cb-36a69c5894b8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pySHACL and Rudof as benchmark comparison targets" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Snarl's `make bench` target (cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py) benchmarks Snarl against pySHACL and Rudof rather than only micro-benchmarking Snarl in isolation. pySHACL (the Python reference SHACL implementation) is treated as the correctness ground truth — compare_mode() picks ref_name = \"pyshacl\" when available, and other validators' result counts are flagged \"(!=<ref_count>)\" in the summary table when they diverge from it. Rudof (a fast Rust-based SHACL validator) is the speed comparison target — the script prints \"Snarl is Nx faster than {validator}\" whenever Snarl's median time beats a validator's by >=1.5x. Each validator is run RUNS=5 times per fixture with a 60s per-run TIMEOUT, and the median wall-clock time is reported. Evidence: cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py (run_pyshacl, run_rudof, run_snarl, compare_mode, ref_name selection, RUNS/TIMEOUT constants) and CLAUDE.md \"make bench # Build + run benchmark comparison (pySHACL, Rudof, Snarl)\", both added in commit e3955f308e5404ccec96c3b4adc17f7f547f66c7." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T05:17:22Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "pySHACL and Rudof as benchmark comparison targets" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8377dad1-27a8-4cef-8da1-4deed480443c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "slop-rdf as the RDF layer dependency" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Snarl depends on the sibling library slop-rdf (../slop-rdf) for Turtle parsing, core RDF types (Term, Triple, IndexedGraph), vocabulary constants, XSD datatype support, and RDF list utilities, rather than implementing its own RDF/Turtle layer. Evidence: CLAUDE.md Dependencies section naming slop-rdf and its responsibilities; cli/main.slop imports the `rdf`, `index`, and `ttl` modules for Term/Triple/Graph/IndexedGraph/parse-ttl-file in this commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "slop-rdf as the RDF layer dependency" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5e0bc84-6fe5-4d25-8d4a-8a9f78a25922> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4e7fb87f-7bd0-4889-b94a-1e3cf4f66832> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF 1.2 quoted-triple Term support" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Snarl's own hand-written SLOP source now exhaustively handles slop-rdf's new `term-triple` Term variant (RDF 1.2 / RDF-star quoted triples), alongside term-literal/term-iri/term-blank, instead of leaving it an unhandled match case. `term-string-value` (src/constraints/string.slop:39-55) coerces a `term-triple` to the empty string, matching the existing blank-node behavior — no lexical string form is defined for a structured triple term, same treatment as a blank node. `term-to-display-string` (src/report.slop:262-300) instead gives it a distinct human-readable form, recursively rendering `<<( subject predicate object )>>` by calling itself on the wrapped triple's subject/predicate/object. This is exercised by a new fixture, cli/tests/fixtures/rdf12-annotation-valid.ttl, and cli/tests/test-cli.slop's test-rdf12-annotation-block, which parses a data graph containing an RDF 1.2 `{| ex:source ex:import |}` annotation block on a triple, asserts it indexes to exactly 17 triples, and asserts the graph still conforms — confirming annotation-block reification triples flow through Snarl's SHACL evaluation like any other triples, with no SHACL Core semantics attached to the annotation itself. Evidence: commit 1f2e74d999405acb1b21d63cbb188a9397ff2ecd (\"rebuild for slop-rdf improvements\") diffs to src/constraints/string.slop (new `((term-triple _) (== $result \"\"))` @post arm and matching `((term-triple _) \"\")` match arm) and src/report.slop (new `((term-triple tt) ...)` arm building `<<( ... )>>` via list-push), plus the new fixture/test pair in cli/tests/test-cli.slop and cli/tests/fixtures/rdf12-annotation-valid.ttl." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:07:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF 1.2 quoted-triple Term support" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d9e4749d-dcc5-4d00-8b82-472a9fcb6dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b0286a15-ec2a-4b6b-b39a-d89b5ee16c52> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "crate-publish performs a real cargo publish, not a dry run" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Makefile's `crate-publish` target now runs `cargo publish --allow-dirty` instead of `cargo publish --dry-run --allow-dirty` — `make crate-publish` will actually publish the `snarl-shacl` crate to crates.io rather than only simulating it. Evidence: Makefile diff in this commit, `crate-publish: crate-vendor` target body changing from `cd rust && cargo publish --dry-run --allow-dirty` to `cd rust && cargo publish --allow-dirty`. No commit message or comment states the rationale; the diff itself is the only evidence — this is recorded as the observable policy change, not an inferred motivation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-28T22:30:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e3d02987-e29b-4ade-948a-84f2e625369f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "crate-publish performs a real cargo publish, not a dry run" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust crate renamed to snarl-shacl, lib output stays snarl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Rust crate's published package identity changes from `snarl` to `snarl-shacl` (rust/Cargo.toml `[package] name`, mirrored in rust/Cargo.lock), while a new `[lib]\\nname = \"snarl\"` block is added to keep the compiled library/crate import name as `snarl` — so downstream code still writes `use snarl::...` and the crate's linked output artifact keeps the `snarl` name, even though its crates.io package id is now different. Everything else about the prior decision (vendoring pre-transpiled csrc/ into rust/csrc/ via `make crate-vendor`, compiling from source via the `cc` build-dependency in rust/build.rs, rather than linking against build/libsnarl.a) is unchanged by this commit — only the published package name and the explicit `[lib]` name override are new. Evidence: commit 1f2e74d999405acb1b21d63cbb188a9397ff2ecd (\"rebuild for slop-rdf improvements\") diff to rust/Cargo.toml (`-name = \"snarl\"` / `+name = \"snarl-shacl\"` under `[package]`, plus new `[lib]\\nname = \"snarl\"` block) and rust/Cargo.lock (`-name = \"snarl\"` / `+name = \"snarl-shacl\"` in the local package entry). No commit message body or code comment states why the package was renamed; only the mechanical rename + lib-name override is evidenced, so no external cause (e.g. a crates.io name collision) is asserted here." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:07:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rust crate renamed to snarl-shacl, lib output stays snarl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust crate vendors pre-transpiled C sources for cargo build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The `rust/` crate (Rust bindings for Snarl, published as the `snarl` crate on crates.io) builds by copying the top-level pre-transpiled `csrc/` sources into `rust/csrc/` via a new `make crate-vendor` target (`cp csrc/src/*.c csrc/src/*.h rust/csrc/src/`; `cp csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h rust/csrc/runtime/`), then compiling them from source at `cargo build` time using the `cc` build-dependency (rust/build.rs lists all slop_*.c sources plus rust/csrc_shim.c, invokes `cc::Build` with `SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP`/`SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE` defines, and links the result into the crate) — rather than linking the crate against the `make lib`-built libsnarl.a directly. `rust/csrc/` is added to .gitignore (generated, not checked in), and Cargo.toml's `include` list only bundles paths inside `rust/` (src/**/*, tests/**/*, csrc/**/*, csrc_shim.c, build.rs, ...) — vendoring into rust/csrc/ is what lets `cargo publish` ship a self-contained package without a path dependency reaching outside the crate root. New Makefile targets `crate-build`/`crate-test`/`crate-publish` all depend on `crate-vendor` running first. Evidence: Makefile crate-vendor/crate-build/crate-test/crate-publish targets, rust/build.rs source list and cc::Build config, rust/Cargo.toml `include` field, .gitignore `rust/csrc` entry — all introduced in commit ee856789f631063db6d116b56793d87b320302e0 (merge PR #1 \"Rustify\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T22:27:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rust crate vendors pre-transpiled C sources for cargo build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f372a5bb-2282-4d93-9da5-7e8d1dc45282> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/88086cbf-ee8d-4436-b22f-f59c690d364e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rudof benchmarked at all fixture scales via minimal output format" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Rudof is no longer skipped at any benchmark fixture scale. benchmark_compare.py drops the RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD=10,000 constant and its skip-check block in compare_mode(), and run_rudof() switches to rudof's `-r minimal` output format, matching results via `re.search(r\"Does not conform,\\s*(\\d+)\\s+violations\", out)` / a literal \"Conforms\" check instead of counting `│`-prefixed table rows. This lets Rudof run and report real numbers at the largest benchmarked scales — employees-100k (494,962 triples) and the newly added meteorites fixture (1,010,109 triples, using the data-only `test_data/large_meteorite_data.ttl` so all three validators can parse the same graph) — both of which the old 10,000-triple threshold would have skipped entirely. Evidence: cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py diff (RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD removal, run_rudof() `-r minimal` + regex rewrite, compare_mode() skip-branch removal) and the updated README.md benchmark table, both in this commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-28T22:30:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rudof benchmarked at all fixture scales via minimal output format" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1162bded-19a0-4615-8c89-0e530b1eac07> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8377dad1-27a8-4cef-8da1-4deed480443c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The public C ABI stayed backward compatible (snarl_validate/snarl_validate_with_config/snarl_conforms unchanged in signature) at the cost of an internal IndexedGraph->SnarlDataGraph conversion for callers who don't use the new snarl_validate_data_graph* entry points." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T19:18:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1bca43f5-c4fe-4406-8199-9e200b522d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The public C ABI stayed backward compatible (snarl_validate/snarl_validate_with_config/snarl_conforms unchanged in signature) at the cost of an internal IndexedGraph->SnarlDataGraph conversion for callers who don't use the new snarl_validate_data_graph* entry points." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2d0c8898-a534-4606-b0d3-980c57f81eb2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
