<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The prior same-file-reuse optimization is lost: cli/main.slop previously special-cased `(if (string-eq shapes-path data-path) (some data-graph) (load-graph arena shapes-path quiet))` to skip re-parsing when the same file was used as both data and shapes; this commit removes that branch entirely (`(let ((shapes-result (load-graph arena shapes-path quiet))) ...)`), because the data graph and shapes graph are now different, incompatible types (SnarlDataGraph vs IndexedGraph) that cannot share one loaded value — a file used as both --shapes and data is now parsed twice." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T19:18:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/792fb302-6853-4956-862c-e25052e45ecd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "The prior same-file-reuse optimization is lost: cli/main.slop previously special-cased `(if (string-eq shapes-path data-path) (some data-graph) (load-graph arena shapes-path quiet))` to skip re-parsing when the same file was used as both data and shapes; this commit removes that branch entirely (`(let ((shapes-result (load-graph arena shapes-path quiet))) ...)`), because the data graph and shapes graph are now different, incompatible types (SnarlDataGraph vs IndexedGraph) that cannot share one loaded value — a file used as both --shapes and data is now parsed twice." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8377dad1-27a8-4cef-8da1-4deed480443c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8377dad1-27a8-4cef-8da1-4deed480443c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rudof is skipped for any fixture above RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD=10,000 triples (the generated 100k-employee fixture), so at that scale only pySHACL and Snarl are compared." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
