<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/11087954-2461-47be-81be-d71bb3fd3623> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/11087954-2461-47be-81be-d71bb3fd3623> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/11087954-2461-47be-81be-d71bb3fd3623> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "check-class (src/constraints/value-type.slop) now treats a value node as satisfying sh:class when it has rdf:type of the required class OR any transitive rdfs:subClassOf of it, not just a direct rdf:type triple match. Implemented via a new shared helper `is-shacl-instance-of-class` (src/target.slop, exported, :c-name snarl_is_shacl_instance_of_class), which reuses the existing `find-subclasses` BFS helper (previously only used by sh:targetClass/implicit-class target resolution) to enumerate class-term plus all transitive subclasses, then checks rdf:type against each. check-class's body changes from a single indexed-graph-contains check against one rdf:type triple to `(if (is-shacl-instance-of-class arena data-graph value-node required-class) (none) (some ...))`.\n\nBefore this commit, sh:class constraint CHECKING (as opposed to sh:targetClass target RESOLUTION, which already had subclass reasoning) only matched a value node against the exact required class IRI — a value typed as a subclass of the required class incorrectly violated sh:class. Evidence: src/constraints/value-type.slop diff removing the direct `indexed-graph-contains data-graph type-triple` check in check-class; src/target.slop diff adding `is-shacl-instance-of-class`. New regression fixtures cli/tests/fixtures/subclass-class-conforms-{data,shapes}.ttl and subclass-class-{data,shapes}.ttl (direct subclass, transitive 2-level subclass, and unrelated-class cases), exercised by cli/tests/test-cli.slop's test-subclass-class-conforms and test-subclass-class (asserts exactly 1 violation, for the unrelated-class value only).\n\nConsequence: sh:class constraint checking and sh:targetClass/implicit-class target resolution now both reason over the same SHACL-instance-of-class relation (rdf:type C or transitive rdfs:subClassOf C), reusing the same find-subclasses BFS helper rather than duplicating subclass-walking logic." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/11087954-2461-47be-81be-d71bb3fd3623> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
