<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "POSIX-only shell tooling for macOS compatibility" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Shell scripts in this repo — starting with cli/tests/w3c/run-w3c-tests.sh — must avoid GNU-only bash/grep extensions, because macOS ships bash 3.2 (no `declare -A` associative-array support, which arrived in bash 4) and BSD grep (no `-P`/PCRE support, a GNU grep extension). This commit removes the \"Load xfail list into associative array\" block that built an `XFAILS` associative array via `declare -A` and looked entries up with `${XFAILS[$testid]+_}`, replacing it with a direct `grep -qxF \"$testid\" \"$XFAIL_FILE\"` line lookup. It also replaces three `grep -oP` capture-group extractions with portable equivalents: the two `sht:dataGraph`/`sht:shapesGraph` `<...>` reference extractions move from `grep -oP '...' | grep -oP '<[^>]+>' | tr -d '<>'` to `sed -n 's/.../\\1/p'`, and the `sh:conforms true/false` alternate-format detection moves from `grep -oP` to `grep -oE` (POSIX extended regex, no capture group needed for a plain true/false match). Evidence: cli/tests/w3c/run-w3c-tests.sh diff in commit 8b89fa738a1e7f0616a06c3c18e931aa9901dfbb (\"workflow fix for mac\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-18T01:25:27Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c3d3ae7c-f20e-421b-a15c-bd14e67dad75> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "POSIX-only shell tooling for macOS compatibility" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Subclass-aware class targeting" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5e966764-26ca-4a63-ac5d-06637b1143fc> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Both explicit sh:targetClass targeting and implicit class targeting (a shape whose IRI is itself used as an rdf:type class) now perform rdfs:subClassOf reasoning: they include instances of transitive subclasses of the target class, not just direct instances. Implemented via a new BFS helper `find-subclasses` (src/target.slop) that walks rdfs:subClassOf edges from class-term outward; `resolve-target-class` now unions rdf:type instances across class-term plus all discovered subclasses (dedup via a seen-set), and `resolve-implicit-class-targets` now delegates to `resolve-target-class` instead of doing a bare rdf:type lookup. Evidence: src/target.slop diff (find-subclasses, resolve-target-class, resolve-implicit-class-targets) in commit aafaa4acec1e29ab1b5202874a4de239c241ecff; the same commit's cli/tests/w3c/xfail.txt removes the `targets/targetClassImplicit-001.ttl` xfail entry that previously documented this gap." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Subclass-aware class targeting" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "List-priority path node parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When a SHACL path node in the shapes graph exhibits both RDF-list structure (rdf:first/rdf:rest) and sh:inversePath (or other SHACL path properties) simultaneously, `parse-path` (src/parse.slop) now treats it as a sequence path — the RDF-list check runs first in the `cond`, ahead of the sh:inversePath / sh:alternativePath / sh:zeroOrMorePath / sh:oneOrMorePath / sh:zeroOrOnePath checks that previously ran first with list-detection as the final fallback. This establishes a deterministic priority (list structure wins) instead of leaving the ambiguous case unhandled. Evidence: src/parse.slop diff in commit aafaa4acec1e29ab1b5202874a4de239c241ecff — the `;; RDF list (sequence path) — takes priority over SHACL path properties` block was moved from the trailing `(true ...)` fallback branch to the first `cond` clause, with the comment \"must be first, as a blank node may have both rdf:first/rdf:rest AND sh:inversePath\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "List-priority path node parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/d9a21834-2294-4d2f-b5f3-5b70ad3e72cd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/75401fe7-6e13-4169-9d69-fdabeb1fdd7d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Implicit class targeting lacks subclass reasoning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "As of this commit, implicit class targeting (a shape that is itself an rdfs:Class/owl:Class used as a target) does not perform rdfs:subClassOf reasoning — it does not expand to instances of subclasses of the shape. Evidence: cli/tests/w3c/xfail.txt in commit b14fe6bfca792ae4b9799d14af7cb5235e4893b8 keeps `targets/targetClassImplicit-001.ttl` xfailed with the comment \"Implicit class targeting needs rdfs:subClassOf reasoning\" (previously a vaguer \"Implicit class targeting edge case\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T01:40:39Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Implicit class targeting lacks subclass reasoning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/dab0b994-d4b3-479a-aebb-aedb8069f823> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/c8783525-b569-4e8c-8c63-19e9affb5f33> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Static inline arena functions need a C shim for Rust FFI linkage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop_arena_new, slop_arena_free, and slop_intern_string are declared `static inline` in slop_runtime.h, so they get inlined at each C call site and never produce an exported/linkable symbol — Rust's FFI can only call functions that have a real symbol, so rust/src/ffi.rs cannot declare `extern \"C\"` bindings straight to them. rust/csrc_shim.c adds thin non-inline wrapper functions (snarl_arena_new, snarl_arena_free, snarl_intern_string) with real extern symbols, which ffi.rs declares and lib.rs calls instead. Evidence: rust/csrc_shim.c header comment, verbatim: \"These are static inline in the header, so they have no exported symbol. We wrap them here so Rust can link to them.\" Added in commit ee856789f631063db6d116b56793d87b320302e0 (merge PR #1 \"Rustify\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T22:27:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Static inline arena functions need a C shim for Rust FFI linkage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/1b18a0e8-0c3a-4665-9a81-ccce24f2c17b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ffc2f0f2-bb27-4920-a708-d159c184b7eb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use native Clang for macOS scale-suite releases" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Run the resource-heavy release test suite with native Apple Clang on macOS ARM runners, while retaining GCC coverage on Ubuntu. GitHub Actions runs 31286152905 and 31287635375 both built the macOS test binary successfully with Homebrew GCC 14 and then killed it with signal 9 / exit 137 after roughly 28-31 seconds. The second run included arena resets before and between the 3,000-node, 1,000-node, and 50,000-node regressions, proving retained allocations from earlier tests were not the complete cause. On the same ARM macOS architecture, the exact commands `make test CC=clang`, `make w3c-test CC=clang`, and `make release CC=clang SNARL_VERSION=0.4.2` complete successfully, including all 46 integration tests and the full 50,000-node fixture. The release workflow therefore selects `clang` for macos-14 and `gcc` for ubuntu-latest, and no longer installs gcc@14 through Homebrew." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-09T01:13:55.546282Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Use native Clang for macOS scale-suite releases" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Isolate scale regressions with arena resets" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Large integration fixtures must not inherit retained allocations from earlier tests when the suite uses one growable arena. In the v0.4.2 release workflow (GitHub Actions run 31286152905), the macOS ARM test process compiled successfully but was killed with signal 9 / exit 137 after the hostile-shapes suite was added; the Ubuntu matrix job was then cancelled rather than independently failing. cli/tests/test-cli.slop ran all 46 tests inside one 64 MB with-arena compiled with SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP, so overflow blocks from completed tests remained live before the 3,000-node, 1,000-node, and 50,000-node scale fixtures. Resetting the test arena before and between those independent scale regressions preserves the full fixtures while releasing prior overflow blocks. Evidence: reset-test-arena and its four calls in cli/tests/test-cli.slop, regenerated in csrc/src/slop_test_cli.c; local verification passed all 46 integration tests, all 98 W3C tests, the optimized 0.4.2 release build/package path, and Rust tests." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-09T01:03:38.344608Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Isolate scale regressions with arena resets" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/b51df32d-1fd6-4747-ad5c-771a2ca49d97> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/35898932-251a-4193-8aaa-7448c7aaf366> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SLOP verifier gaps found while hardening @post/@property" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "While tightening @post and @property contracts to match the new executable @example forms, several categories of predicate could not be verified by `slop verify` even though they are true, and had to be reformulated or annotated in place with a `;; VERIFIER: ...` comment explaining why, rather than silently left as-is. Concrete gaps found: (1) helper functions like `term-eq` and `xsd-compare` carry no @post axiom of their own, so the verifier can't bridge their result into a Z3-provable equality/ordering fact at call sites (string.slop check-has-value/check-in, other.slop check-closed, value-range.slop check-min/max-inclusive/exclusive); (2) a callee's local @post is not usable as an axiom by its caller, and struct/record fields don't propagate through an `(some ...)` wrapper, so postconditions comparing into wrapped record fields fail to translate (string.slop check-min-length/check-max-length); (3) `list-push` mutates its list argument in place, so a @post that compares `$result`'s field against a \"before\" snapshot of the same (now-aliased) list is vacuously true, not a real check (types.slop report-add-result); (4) loop-bound properties (e.g. `bounded-results`) can't be proven without an explicit loop invariant relating a `set-has` membership predicate to `list-len` (string.slop check-unique-lang). Evidence: `;; VERIFIER: ...` comments introduced in this commit's diff to src/constraints/string.slop, src/constraints/value-range.slop, src/constraints/other.slop, and src/types.slop (commit aafaa4acec1e29ab1b5202874a4de239c241ecff)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fc12b574-8856-48c9-88ca-5f34706c92f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SLOP verifier gaps found while hardening @post/@property" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seeded synthetic employee benchmark fixtures" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Benchmark fixtures at 1k/10k/100k employee scale are generated programmatically (generate_benchmark() in cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py, invoked via `--generate`) rather than hand-written or sampled from real data. Generation uses a fixed random.seed(42) for reproducibility and targets ~20% of records with SHACL violations, split across four types keyed on one `r = random.random()` draw per employee: r<0.05 omits ex:name (minCount violation), 0.05<=r<0.10 sets an underage ex:age of 10-17 (minInclusive violation), 0.10<=r<0.15 writes a malformed ex:email missing \"@\" (pattern violation), and 0.15<=r<0.20 writes ex:department as a string literal instead of an ex: IRI (nodeKind + class violation, counted as 2). Shapes are copied from the existing fixtures/employee-dir-shapes.ttl rather than authoring new benchmark-specific shapes. Evidence: cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py generate_benchmark() and the FIXTURES list referencing fixtures/benchmarks/employees-{1k,10k,100k}-*.ttl, plus the generated cli/tests/fixtures/benchmarks/employees-100k-data.ttl output, all added in commit e3955f308e5404ccec96c3b4adc17f7f547f66c7. Used by the \"pySHACL and Rudof as benchmark comparison targets\" ArchitecturalDecision (https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/cd10b208-5d0b-4e26-a462-b07e3fd6d790)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T05:17:22Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/063c28ac-192a-44b0-b731-01d972bfec20> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Seeded synthetic employee benchmark fixtures" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Arena-only allocation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "All allocation across the engine and public API goes through arena allocators (an Arena parameter is threaded through validate/validate-with-config/report-to-graph/report-to-string); there is no manual/individual memory management. Evidence: CLAUDE.md Conventions \"Arena-based allocation — no manual memory management\"; the Public API table shows every allocating function taking an Arena as its first parameter." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/0f71c21b-1582-4c39-8b92-c7d502507c54> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Arena-only allocation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Full contract annotations on functions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every function carries a full contract — @intent, @spec, @pre, @post, @property, @example, @alloc — as both documentation and a partially machine-checkable correctness discipline. Evidence: CLAUDE.md Conventions \"Full contracts on all functions: @intent, @spec, @pre, @post, @property, @example, @alloc\"; cli/main.slop functions (e.g. print-elapsed) carry @intent/@spec annotations in this commit's diff." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/48c3593d-2a5c-4194-9a13-dfb3aa3af141> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Full contract annotations on functions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "snarl_* C FFI naming convention" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every public SLOP function is declared with `:c-name \"snarl_*\"` so the compiled library exposes a stable, namespaced C API, documented in include/snarl.h, safe for external C consumers to link against directly. Evidence: CLAUDE.md Conventions \"All public functions use :c-name \\\"snarl_*\\\" for stable C FFI\"; Public API table (snarl_validate, snarl_conforms, snarl_get_violations, etc.) introduced in this commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5e0b28bc-d765-48b7-b33a-cf1f44c6a8f7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "snarl_* C FFI naming convention" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Predicate-extraction for provable @post contracts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Across src/constraints/value-type.slop, value-range.slop, string.slop, and other.slop, several constraint-check functions now extract their pass/fail boolean logic into a small named pure helper (e.g. `min-inclusive-satisfied`/`max-inclusive-satisfied`/`min-exclusive-satisfied`/`max-exclusive-satisfied` in value-range.slop, `datatype-matches`/`node-kind-matches` in value-type.slop, `min-length-satisfied`/`max-length-satisfied` in string.slop, `list-contains-term` in other.slop). Each helper is called both inside the function's `if` branch AND inside its `@post`/`@property` as `(== (== $result (none)) (helper-fn ...))` — a single uninterpreted-predicate-call form that is trivially provable by construction, instead of asking the verifier to re-derive the same boolean from inline match/cond logic (e.g. an inline `xsd-compare` match across 4 arms).\n\nThis directly resolves several of the concrete verifier gaps recorded in the earlier \"SLOP verifier gaps found while hardening @post/@property\" Lesson: gap (1) (helper functions like xsd-compare/term-eq carrying no @post of their own, blocking the verifier from bridging results at call sites) for value-range.slop's check-min/max-inclusive/exclusive and other.slop's check-has-value/check-in; gap (2) (record fields not propagating through an Option wrapper) for string.slop's check-min-length/check-max-length. Evidence: this commit's diff removes 9 `;; VERIFIER: \"Could not translate\"/\"fails\"...` workaround comments (value-range.slop x4, other.slop x2, string.slop x2, plus one more) that had documented these exact unprovable postconditions, replacing each with the extract-and-reference-helper form. The resolution is partial, not complete: VERIFIER comments for a different gap category remain at HEAD in src/constraints/pair.slop (resolve-path/xsd-compare), string.slop's check-unique-lang (gap 4, an unprovable loop-bound invariant), and other.slop's check-closed (term-eq/path-predicate destructuring) — none of those were touched by this commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:07:26Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/adad7da1-27b8-4bd2-b519-e2728fede947> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Predicate-extraction for provable @post contracts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cycle-safe recursive shape evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Shape evaluation is recursive (shapes reference other shapes through sh:node, sh:property, and logical constraints) and is protected against cycles in the shapes graph by tracking a visited set during evaluation. Evidence: CLAUDE.md Conventions \"Recursive shape evaluation with cycle detection via visited set\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T21:02:18Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b8e27b1d-bcdf-4f6e-8bd7-780b81323700> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Cycle-safe recursive shape evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sibling qualified-value-shape refs for disjoint counting" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "To support sh:qualifiedValueShapesDisjoint, evaluate-node-shape-cached (src/engine.slop) first scans all non-deactivated property shapes on a node shape for `con-qualified-value-shape` constraints with disjoint=true, collecting each (property-shape-id, qvs-ref) pair. It then, per property shape, builds a `sibling-qvs-refs` list of every OTHER disjoint sibling's qvs-ref, and threads that list down through evaluate-property-shape(-cached) and evaluate-constraint-for-property(-cached) as a new parameter. The qualified-value-shape constraint check then excludes, from its own conforming-value count, any value that already conforms to a sibling ref (see the `disjoint`/`conforms-to-sibling` branch in evaluate-constraint-for-property-cached). This required adding a `sibling_qvs_refs` parameter to the corresponding C signatures. Evidence: src/engine.slop and csrc/src/slop_engine.c diff in commit b14fe6bfca792ae4b9799d14af7cb5235e4893b8." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T01:40:39Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/de1ce679-8cc8-48d3-bd54-d99fe0ab2bdb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Sibling qualified-value-shape refs for disjoint counting" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Executable fixture-backed @example contracts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Function `@example` annotations are now structured, executable forms — real argument expressions built from constructors (make-iri, make-literal, make-triple) and small per-module `fixture-*` helper functions (e.g. fixture-g-alice-name, fixture-allowed-langs, fixture-term-list-ab) — rather than inert string-literal doc-comments describing a call in prose (e.g. the old `(@example \"(check-min-inclusive arena focus (term-literal 5 xsd:integer) ...) -> (none)\")`). Each affected module gains a `;; Test URI constants` block (EX_FOCUS, EX_SHAPE, etc.) and a `;; Test Fixtures` section of small graph/list-building functions used only by @example forms. Evidence: src/path.slop, src/target.slop, src/parse.slop, src/constraints/string.slop, src/constraints/value-range.slop, src/constraints/other.slop, src/report.slop, src/snarl.slop, src/types.slop diffs in commit aafaa4acec1e29ab1b5202874a4de239c241ecff — every changed @example in these files converts from a string literal to a parenthesized argument-expression form, several evaluating to a real return-value assertion (`-> (some 42)`)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/e036662f-a78f-43b0-9d2c-f08a924fa619> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Executable fixture-backed @example contracts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Raw ffi module plus safe wrapper module for Rust bindings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The `snarl` Rust crate splits FFI concerns into two layers: rust/src/ffi.rs holds only raw `extern \"C\"` declarations and `#[repr(C)]` structs/unions/enums that mirror the C ABI in snarl.h/slop_runtime.h exactly (e.g. SlopString, the RdfTerm tagged union, ValidatorResultFfi) with no safety wrapping; rust/src/lib.rs then provides the safe public API (Arena, IndexedGraph, validate, ValidatorResult, Severity, etc.) built on top of ffi.rs, converting to/from the raw types via helpers like term_to_ffi and slop_string_to_str. Evidence: rust/src/ffi.rs module doc \"Raw FFI bindings matching the C types in `snarl.h` and `slop_runtime.h`.\"; rust/src/lib.rs module doc \"Safe Rust bindings for the Snarl SHACL Core validator.\" with a doctest example built on Arena/IndexedGraph/validate. Both added in commit ee856789f631063db6d116b56793d87b320302e0 (merge PR #1 \"Rustify\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T22:27:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f57631d7-80c5-4f57-8dc9-d921731163d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Raw ffi module plus safe wrapper module for Rust bindings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: List-priority path node parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior Constraint recorded this exact ambiguous case (RDF-list structure plus sh:inversePath on the same path node) as unsupported, citing xfail.txt keeping path-strange-002.ttl xfailed. This commit resolves the ambiguity by reordering parse-path's cond so list-detection runs before the inversePath check, giving list structure priority — and the same commit's xfail.txt diff drops the path-strange-002.ttl entry. The fix and the removal of its own evidence-of-absence land together, so this supersedes rather than extends the prior record." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/47cf34b3-a2e6-4b68-bdc4-dcda9f399948> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: List-priority path node parsing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Rust crate renamed to snarl-shacl, lib output stays snarl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 1f2e74d999405acb1b21d63cbb188a9397ff2ecd retires the specific package-name fact from the prior decision (\"published as the `snarl` crate on crates.io\") by renaming the package to `snarl-shacl` in rust/Cargo.toml and rust/Cargo.lock. The vendoring build mechanism the prior decision actually describes (crate-vendor copying csrc/ into rust/csrc/, cc-based compilation in build.rs) is untouched by this diff, but the record's stated package identity is now stale, so the record is superseded with an updated description rather than left inaccurate." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-25T20:07:02Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4fc57d92-62e1-426c-a258-99d8d4484f93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Rust crate renamed to snarl-shacl, lib output stays snarl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Rudof benchmarked at all fixture scales via minimal output format" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior consequence (RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD=10,000 triples, above which Rudof was skipped in compare_mode()) is retired directly by this commit's diff to cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py: the RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD constant and the `if vname == \"rudof\" and triples > RUDOF_SKIP_THRESHOLD: ... SKIPPED` branch are both deleted outright. In the same diff, run_rudof() switches its invocation from `rudof shacl-validate -s shapes data` (parsed by scraping table rows and matching \"No Errors found\") to `rudof shacl-validate -r minimal -s shapes data` (parsed via regex against \"Conforms\" / \"Does not conform, N violations\"). The updated README table in this commit shows real Rudof numbers (not \"—\") at the employees-100k (494,962 triples) and new meteorites (1,010,109 triples) rows, both well above the old 10,000-triple skip threshold — confirming the skip was actually removed, not just the constant left unused." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-28T22:30:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/bbeafa9f-bd5a-4517-9138-287ab3e83520> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Rudof benchmarked at all fixture scales via minimal output format" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Use native Clang for macOS scale-suite releases" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The first lesson concluded that arena isolation addressed the constrained-runner failure. The retagged v0.4.2 run at commit 95934e2 included that isolation yet reproduced the same macOS GCC 14 signal-9 termination, so the earlier causal conclusion was incomplete and must be replaced with the compiler/platform-specific evidence." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-09T01:13:55.546282Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f75f63f3-62fe-4a91-b1a5-b8db70b13d7e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Use native Clang for macOS scale-suite releases" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Subclass-aware class targeting" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior Constraint recorded that implicit class targeting had no rdfs:subClassOf reasoning, citing xfail.txt keeping targetClassImplicit-001.ttl xfailed as evidence of the gap. This commit closes that gap directly: target.slop adds find-subclasses and rewires resolve-target-class/resolve-implicit-class-targets to use it, and the same commit's xfail.txt diff drops the targetClassImplicit-001.ttl entry — the fix and the removal of its own evidence-of-absence land together, so this supersedes rather than merely extends the prior record." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/fb2f3903-4acc-48b1-9916-8a46bd19e72d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-14T03:43:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
